  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In Shang clan city, Old Zhang reports that San Cha Mountain has found how to enter the three kings inheritance ground, and he names King Bao’s inheritance among the three pillar shares.",
      "chapters": [
        324
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_shang_clan_city",
        "loc_san_cha_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The inheritance interior sits in a Gu Immortal blessed land small world rather than in the main world. At initial entry, heavenly power leaves only the rank one key Gu usable, matching the pattern of King Quan Inheritance and King Xin Inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        346
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-label",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "inh_king_quan_inheritance",
        "inh_king_xin_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Among the three kings, King Bao is a fire path Gu Master, and the inheritance is built to choose inheritors of that path.",
      "chapters": [
        347
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "path-label",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_king_bao",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the peaks the red light pillar marks this entrance beside the yellow and blue pillars of the other two kings.",
      "chapters": [
        352
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "peak-pillars",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yi Huo reserves King Bao Inheritance; he is fire path, King Bao is of the same path, and he faces Kong Ri Tian, Long Qing Tian, and Yi Chong when those three attack together on San Cha Mountain. Wu Shen Tong watches with fear of Yi Huo’s reputation but does not join that three-man assault. Yi Huo answers with a vast flame display that covers the water wave, burns the poison palm, and drives the phoenix winged golden butterflies back, and onlookers name his rank five Gu prairie fire before he walks into the red pillar. Kong Ri Tian and Long Qing Tian afterward enter King Xin Inheritance; Wu Shen Tong and Yi Chong enter King Quan Inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        356
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "flame-clash-at-the-red-pillar",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_yi_huo",
        "char_kong_ri_tian",
        "char_long_qing_tian",
        "char_yi_chong",
        "char_wu_shen_tong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing enter together, Fang Yuan sees a grey-white sky and light red ground of volcanic rock, steam, and grey dust. Baby-sized red eggmen with round red eggs on their chests come out of volcanic rock houses and call the place Hong Dan village while attacking the “demon king.” The inheritance’s aim in that round is to make the Gu Master use exploding egg Gu to exterminate those red eggmen and advance.",
      "chapters": [
        376
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "interior-eggmen",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "loc_hong_dan_village",
        "gu_exploding_egg_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo Wu Tian names King Bao as Wang Ba Dan and says he had eight egg empresses and produced numerous eggmen as part of the essence of the three kings inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "stone-door",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_mo_wu_tian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xiao Mang reaches a tall stone door and says that blowing it apart will obtain King Bao’s final inheritance, then concludes light path lacks the fire type destructive power the door wants and abandons that door when a Gu Immortal treasure is reported in the fog.",
      "chapters": [
        392
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "stone-door",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xiao_mang"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later he is still anxious about the unopened King Bao Inheritance while fighting elsewhere in the blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        402
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "stone-door",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
